# Blue Oak Revenue Infrastructure™ — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values before running or deploying.
# NEVER commit .env to version control — it is listed in .gitignore.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: Vite environment variables prefixed with VITE_ are
# embedded in the client bundle at build time and are visible to
# anyone who inspects the built JavaScript.
#
# Treat VITE_LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL and VITE_BOOKING_URL as semi-public
# endpoints, not secrets. Protect the receiving services through
# server-side validation, rate limiting, and duplicate detection —
# not by assuming the URL is hidden.
#
# If webhook secrecy is required, introduce a server-side proxy
# (e.g. a Vercel or Netlify edge function) that holds the real
# URL and forwards validated payloads.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LEAD WEBHOOK ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Make.com (or compatible) webhook URL for lead delivery.
# Both the Contact message form and Revenue Snapshot form POST here.
# The receiving Make scenario should:
#   - Validate required fields
#   - Reject honeypot-filled submissions (__hp must be empty)
#   - Deduplicate by email or phone
#   - Route to Airtable and send Blue Oak notification
#
# Example: https://hook.eu2.make.com/YOUR_SCENARIO_ID
VITE_LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── BOOKING URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Calendar Appointment Scheduling page URL.
# This is the real booking page visitors and Maya will use.
# When set, the Contact and Revenue Snapshot pages display a
# "View Available Times" button linking to this URL.
# When not set, those pages display a fallback message.
#
# Google Calendar controls actual availability, timezone handling,
# conflict prevention, and confirmation. Do not recreate those
# functions in React.
#
# Setup:
#   1. In Google Calendar, create an Appointment Schedule
#      named "Blue Oak Revenue Infrastructure Consultation"
#      (recommended: 30 minutes, Google Meet enabled)
#   2. Publish the booking page
#   3. Paste the booking page URL here
#
# Example: https://calendar.google.com/calendar/appointments/schedules/YOUR_SCHEDULE_ID
VITE_BOOKING_URL=
